## When you are done

1. Verify each claim in the code before you change anything. Items come from static analysis and a reviewer's notes, so one may be wrong or already fixed. If it is, skip it and say why.
2. Change only what an item calls for. Do not reformat or refactor around it.
3. Run the tests and the build in each repo you changed, and fix what you broke.
4. Reply with one line per item: changed, skipped (why), or needs a decision. End with the test result.
